 "about_text": "MOCA, founded in 1979, is Los Angeles's leading museum dedicated to contemporary art, built around a collection of nearly 8,000 works with deep holdings in LA-based practice alongside international art. MOCA Grand Avenue, the museum's original and flagship site in downtown LA, was designed by architect Arata Isozaki in the 1980s and opened as his first completed US project, announcing MOCA as a major architectural presence on Bunker Hill. The museum also operates The Geffen Contemporary at MOCA, a renovated warehouse in Little Tokyo, and stewards Michael Heizer's land-art work Double Negative in Nevada. Programming spans monographic and thematic exhibitions, education initiatives, publishing, and new-media engagement.",
